>Cutler</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Feighner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Distinct mechanism for antidepressant activity by blockade of central substance P receptors</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1998</year><volume>281</volume><fpage>1640</fpage><lpage>1645</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.281.5383.1640</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kramer MS, Cutler N, Feighner J et al (1998) Distinct mechanism for antidepressant activity by blockade of central substance P receptors. Science 281:1640&#x02013;1645 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9733503</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krishnan</surname><given-names>KRR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical experience with substance P receptor (NK1) antagonists in depression</article-title><source>J Clin Psychiatry</source><year>2002</year><volume>63</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>29</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Krishnan KRR (2002) Clinical experience with substance P receptor (NK1) antagonists in depression. J Clin Psychiatry 63:25&#x02013;29 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12562140</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rupniak</surname><given-names>NM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Elucidating the antidepressant actions of substance P (NK1 receptor) antagonists</article-title><source>Curr Opin Investig Drugs</source><year>2002</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>257</fpage><lpage>261</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Rupniak NM (2002) Elucidating the antidepressant actions of substance P (NK1 receptor) antagonists. Curr Opin Investig Drugs 3:257&#x02013;261 <pub-id pub-id